00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.590 align:start position:0%
 
hello everybody  in this video i'm going to tell you a  bit more about the ongoing auditors  competition for which you can still  register until the 12th of april  now you may have seen on our website on  the landing page of this competition  this particular infographic which shows  you basically in a nutshell  what the different stages are in this  competition  in one blink of an eye  now i will give you a bit more in-depth  information on these different steps  of this infographic all right  so the eligibility criteria first you  need this is an ad7 competition so you  need  a degree being a master's degree  plus six years of experience in the  field  or a bachelor's degree with seven years  of experience in the field  and that experience must be in one of  the  fields that is mentioned below  as you can see audit economics finance  statistics mathematics  data analysis computer engineering or  data mining this has to be the topic of  your work  experience  if you are legible you can apply and  then you see here on this slide at the  different steps of the competition i  will go in in detail in each of them  first there will be of course the  application phase  then there's a first testing stage  then there's a second testing stage  which is the assessment center and once  you've completed that your name if you  are successful will be placed on a list  of people to recruit by the court of  auditors in luxembourg  so let's have a closer look on these  different steps the application goes  through your epso account so you should  have  or you should create an epso account if  you don't have one yet  once you have created your account log  out of it and then go back to our home  page of the website basically where you  can start your application by clicking  on the  audit entry  as i said you can still apply until 12  april 2022  noon brussels time  you have to fill out your application  form in your first language now the  first language is a choice of the 24  official eu languages up to you to  choose which one you you choose  most people take their monotone but you  don't have to if you feel fluid fluent  enough in another language you can  choose any of the 24 available  part of the application process  is already the talent screener which is  the first stage of the testing but you  already  fill out this stage in the application  here  now that part the talent screener part  must be filled out in your second  language  and the second language for this  competition is a choice between either  english or french okay  once you've done that you validate your  application in time and then the first  testing really starts so as i said you  have already completed the talent  screener part this is a set of nine  questions  to basically assess your qualifications  we see which degrees you have which work  experience you have in which fields how  much how long all that  it's a set of nine questions and each  questions question has a certain weight  and you can gain a number of points per  question and of course the best ones the  ones with the most points make it to the  next stage  how many people we invite to the next  stage depends on the number of  successful people that we want to select  through this competition and that number  is 60. so we will invite a maximum of  180  people to the next stage of testing okay  this next stage is part of what we call  the assessment center in the assessment  center we have three different stages or  the three different tests  the first test is a reasoning skills  test  and you see on this slide the number of  questions we ask you the time allocated  to solve these questions  and the points you need  to make it to the next phase basically  for this competition we need you to get  a combined pass mark  of at least 30 out of 50. so you can  fail in one or more  of these reading skills as long as  combined you reach at least 30. okay  this stage is an important stage so i do  advise you to test this to train this  and you can do so on our website we have  sample tests available in all 24  languages  to train these reading skills  because as you can see here it's not  only about the difficulty of the  questions  but there's also this time factor  involved and this makes that you have to  solve these questions in a limited  amount of time which makes it harder to  do  by training this by you know doing this  often you get better at this so please  go to the link  which you see on this slide here and try  this okay  the ones who  reach the past mark they are invited to  the next stage  and the next stage is a couple of  interviews  first of all there's a field related  interview so we test your knowledge in  the field and you need at least 120  points out of 200 so you see this is an  important test because you can get up to  200  points here  you sit this test in your second  language the one you used to fill out  the talent screener so either english or  french  and then we make you sit  two more interviews  to assess your general competencies  first we tested your knowledge in the  field now we're going to test your  general competencies  there's a first interview which we call  the  the competency based interview and there  we test four general competencies you  see them listed here on this slide  you can get 10 points per  per competency  and  combined with the next test which is the  situational competency based interview  you need at least a combined pass mark  of 40 out of 80 because  this situational competency based  interview tests for other general  competencies  also listed on this slide here so we've  got eight competencies in total you can  gain up to 10 points per competency and  you need at least 40 out of 80 combined  again you can fail some but then you  have to perform better on others okay  the situational competency based  interview is basically an interview  where we put you in a certain situation  a work-related situation  and we want to see how you would react  in that given situation that's the  difference with the normal  competency based interview okay  so the best ones make it to the list of  successful candidates and we're looking  for 60  auditors to recruit and the institution  recruiting these 60 auditors will be the  european court of auditors which is  located in luxembourg  so what happens next is as soon as this  list is published the court of orders  will get in touch with  the people on the list and offer them a  position in the months after publication  of that list  so then you can start working  quite soon after that  i hope this is clear  if you have any questions you can always  reach out to us through the contact form  on our website and my colleagues will be  very happy to answer your questions  thank you for your attention and good  luck bye

